VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       POSIX.1‐2001 says: "The only portable use of mmkknnoodd()  is  to  create  a
       FIFO‐special  file.  If _m_o_d_e is not SS__IIFFIIFFOO or _d_e_v is not 0, the behav‐
       ior of mmkknnoodd() is unspecified."  However, nowadays one should never use
       mmkknnoodd() for this purpose; one should use mmkkffiiffoo(3),  a  function  espe‐
       cially defined for this purpose.

       Under  Linux, mmkknnoodd() cannot be used to create directories.  One should
       make directories with mmkkddiirr(2).

